  "claim": "The writer of American Oxygen also worked on a track with the writer of \"Crack a Bottle\"which was released in February 2010. \"Crack a Bottle\" also featured Dr. Dre and 50 Cent.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Alex da Kid. Sentence: He has gained recognition for producing several hit singles for a plethora of artists in various music genres, such as Dr. Dre (\"I Need a Doctor\"), Nicki Minaj (\"Massive Attack\"), B.o.B (\"Airplanes\" featuring Hayley Williams), Eminem (\"Love the Way You Lie\" featuring Rihanna), Diddy (\"Coming Home\" with Dirty Money featuring Skylar Grey), Imagine Dragons (\"Radioactive\") and Cheryl (\"Under The Sun\").\nPage: Love the Way You Lie. Sentence: \"Love the Way You Lie\" is a song recorded by the American rapper Eminem, featuring the Barbadian singer Rihanna, from Eminem's seventh studio album \"Recovery\" (2010).\nPage: American Oxygen. Sentence: It was written by Alex da Kid, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris and Rihanna; Alex da Kid and Kanye West produced it.\nPage: Crack a Bottle. Sentence: \"Crack a Bottle\" is a song by American rapper Eminem, featuring American rappers Dr. Dre and 50 Cent.",
