        "original_id": "5fb2a0ad-a30e-5709-b2f4-4f8867e9eecd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alex da Kid, Eminem, Rihanna, Dr. Dre, Nicki Minaj, B.o.B, Hayley Williams, Diddy, Skylar Grey, Imagine Dragons, Cheryl, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris, Kanye West, 50 Cent\n- Songs: I Need a Doctor, Massive Attack, Airplanes, Love the Way You Lie, Coming Home, Radioactive, Under The Sun, American Oxygen, Crack a Bottle\n- Albums: Recovery\n\nFacts:\n- Alex da Kid gained recognition for producing hit singles across genres, including Dr. Dre's \"I Need a Doctor,\" Nicki Minaj's \"Massive Attack,\" B.o.B's \"Airplanes\" featuring Hayley Williams, Eminem's \"Love the Way You Lie\" featuring Rihanna, Diddy's \"Coming Home\" with Dirty Money featuring Skylar Grey, Imagine Dragons' \"Radioactive,\" and Cheryl's \"Under The Sun.\"\n- \"Love the Way You Lie\" is a song by Eminem featuring Rihanna from Eminem's seventh studio album \"Recovery\" (2010).\n- \"Crack a Bottle\" is a song by Eminem featuring Dr. Dre and 50 Cent.\n- \"American Oxygen\" was written by Alex da Kid, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris, and Rihanna, and it was produced by Alex da Kid and Kanye West.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
